 enteric viruses in Tunisia</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2008</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>1349</fpage><lpage>1355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.02438-07</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18287312</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Keskim&#x000e4;ki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mattila</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Peltola</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Siitonen</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Prevalence of diarrheagenic <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> in Finns with or without diarrhea during a round-the-world trip</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>4425</fpage><lpage>4429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11101575</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hien</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheutz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Cam</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Serichantalergs</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Huong</surname><given-names>TT</given-names></name><name><surname>Thu</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalsgaard</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Diarrheagenic <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> and <italic>Shigella</italic> strains isolated from children in a hospital case&#x02013;control study in Hanoi, Vietnam</article-title><source>J Clin Microbobiol</source><year>2008</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>996</fpage><lpage>1004</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.01219-07</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Okeke</surname><given-names>IN</given-names></name><name><surname>Lamikanra</su